{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most horizons, especially during strong uptrends. Apply an upward level correction (additive) that is larger when recent momentum is positive.",
    "Trend/lag error: the model reacts too slowly to regime shifts; it underestimates the slope during rallies. Use a momentum-based slope boost (e.g., increase daily drift proportional to the last 5–10 day return).",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: errors grow with forecast horizon (mid-to-late window misses the cumulative move). Apply a horizon-scaled uplift (small in days 1–5, larger in days 10–30).",
    "Over-smoothing/mean-reversion bias: forecasts revert toward ~71–76 even when the market breaks out to ~80–84. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making higher highs (trend filter).",
    "Peak/turn timing: after sharp rises, the model often predicts a plateau/soft pullback too early versus continued strength. Delay reversal signals unless there is confirmed negative momentum (e.g., 3–5 consecutive down closes)."
  ]
}
